/P 292 0 R
/E (2.2 ENGAGEMENT WITH GOVERNMENT ON CONTENT MONETISATION)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (ZAMCOPS is in ongoing engagement with Government on the monetisation of Zambian content. The concern is straightforward: Zambian creative work is being used and enjoyed, and its creators should have a fair opportunity to earn from that use.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (These discussions have not been described as a concluded agreement. We will continue to represent the interests of rights holders and report the outcome when concrete arrangements are confirmed.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (2.3 SECRETARIAT TRAINING ON ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (The Society is training its Secretariat to understand artificial intelligence and its implications for our industry. We are looking at the practical benefits of AI for administrative work, while also examining the risks it presents for copyright, authorship, the imitation of performers and the unauthorised use of protected works.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (2.4 MEMBER EDUCATION ON THE COPYRIGHT BILL AND PROPOSED AMENDMENTS)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (ZAMCOPS took part in educating its members on the Copyright Bill and the proposed amendments. A considerable number of members participated, showing that creators want to understand the laws that govern their work and livelihoods.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (This engagement helped bring the legislative discussion closer to the people it affects. It gave members an opportunity to examine the proposals and raise questions. We must continue making room for informed member participation as the legislative process develops.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
