/K [4]
>>
endobj
447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (The discussions addressed royalty obligations, properly licensed music and cooperation between broadcasters and the Society. Radio and television remain major users of music and important channels for promoting local artists. Promotion, however, cannot replace payment for copyright use.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (Accurate music usage records are necessary for identifying works and distributing royalties fairly. Continued cooperation with broadcasting institutions and the Authority is therefore important.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (3. COPYRIGHT LEGISLATION AND POLICY DEVELOPMENTS)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (One of the most important developments during the period under review was the publication of the Copyright and Related Rights Bill, 2025, for stakeholder consultation. The proposed legislation addresses copyright protection, enforcement, collective management and related matters.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
451 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (The Bill attracted interest across the creative industry because of its implications for the ownership, management and commercial use of creative works. ZAMCOPS publicly called for more time for creators and other stakeholders to study the proposals and submit their views.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
452 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (The Board recognises the need for copyright legislation that responds to changes in technology and protects rights holders. Reform must also reflect the practical experience of creators and the institutions responsible for administering their rights. The Society should continue to examine proposed changes carefully and participate in appropriate consultations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (4. MUSIC LICENSING AND COPYRIGHT COMPLIANCE)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (Copyright licensing remains the principal source of revenue for the Society. ZAMCOPS licenses establishments that use copyrighted music commercially, including broadcasters, hotels, restaurants, bars, shops and entertainment venues.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (Compliance among music users remains a serious concern. During the period under review, General Manager Mr. Mirrias Siamutondo publicly stated that fewer than 15 radio stations were complying with licensing requirements out of more than 150 stations operating in the country at the time of his remarks. This was a reported position at that time, not a verified current count.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (When commercial users fail to pay, the funds available for distribution to rights holders are affected. Improving compliance requires continued engagement, appropriate enforcement and clear public education. Buying music for personal use does not automatically authorise its commercial public use.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
